Choate -> NMH[label="4.4
04/11", weight="96", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,St. Marks, Choate, NMH			
Distance: 1500m Conditions: Variable crossing tailwind, 14-17mph with gusts. Lake was protected due to wind direction, and water was good at start, very choppy from 300-600m. Wind shifted speed all afternoon. Comments: G3 started a boat length over the line. Great racing by all crews! We were lucky to have the sunshine.
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=FB4EC0A3A1B57E11BCA0D62F8B29A986&cat=5", random="random"]; 
BelmontHill -> Nobles[label="7.6 (8.77)
05/02", weight="93", tooltip="NEIRA Boys Fours, Belmont Hill vs Nobles, The Bassett Cup & Crawford-Parker JV Cup			
Distance: 1300m Conditions: Steady & strong direct headwind, varying slightly in intensity through the racing. Comments: An epic day of competition! Great racing across the board, with three of the eight races decided by 3.2 seconds or less. Nobles varsity crews take home the Bassett Cup by virtue of their wins in the 1V4 and 3V4; Belmont Hill wins the inaugural Crawford-Parker JV Cup. Thanks to all of the Nobles crews and coaches for an outstanding afternoon/early evening on the Charles!
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=CAF3ECF34078FA9EE5DD65E440E3B490&cat=1", random="random"]; 
