05/09", weight="25", tooltip="NEIRA Boys Fours, Berkshire v. Canterbury, Lyme/Old Lyme			
Distance: 1300 M Conditions: Steady rain; occasional very light tailwind; flat water. Comments: To ensure fair racing, course was shortened from 1500 M due to aggressive weed growth in the starting area.
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=09397F83C568CCDDD278C059BD735052&cat=1", random="random"]; 
Hotchkiss -> Hopkins[label="32.7
05/16", weight="68", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,Hopkins, Hotchkiss, Notre DameHousatonic Sprints			
Distance: 1500 Conditions: Sunny and beautiful morning, light quartering tailwind about 6mph, increasing to 9mph by the last race. Floating start. Comments: Boats raced top down, interleaving boys and girls heats. In the B1 race both Hotchkiss and Hopkins pushed starboard towards Notre Dame's lane, which eventually pinched the Notre Dame boat and caused it to hit the 1000m buoy. Notre Dame came to a stop and lost time untangling. The incident affected the Notre Dame B1 margin.
Thank you, Hotchkiss and Notre Dame for coming and enjoying the day with us! We look forward to hosting you again next year!
None", URL="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=9E09E22A943FD9337DBC41A86B19FC0E&cat=5", random="random"]; 
Nobles -> Groton[label="0.5 (0.56)
04/18", weight="100", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,BB&N vs. Groton and Nobles			
Distance: 1350 Conditions: Good conditions overall with a light crosswind that was consistent throughout the day Comments: Great racing all around and thanks to Groton and Nobles for making the trip. In the boys 4th boat, Nobles paddled shortly before they crossed line. In the girls 2nd boat, Groton veered into BB&N's lane before the first bridge and they clashed oars, then again after the bridge causing BB&N to steer to avoid another clash. Nobles JV also made the trip and the 7th and 8th boats raced BB&N on the half mile course just upstream of Eliot Bridge. Results for those races:
B7 (raced as an 8): 
Nobles
BB&N
G7:
Nobles
BB&N
G8:
BB&N
Nobles
